Honestly, most of this would wash over me. I'm not reading small print on a crisp packet at quarter to eleven with a van full of bins outside. The calorie numbers are the only bit I'd notice, because you can compare a fruit pot's 95 against a Dairy Milk's 240 in one glance. The shock photos might make me stop for a second, but I'd probably think it was a bit much, and I'd still want the Galaxy.

